      "args": {
        "var": "HHDI_ADDFACTOR",
        "shock": 1637.5,
        "periods": 12
      },
      "cost": "cheap",
      "local_cheap": true,
      "quoted_at": "obr/index.html",
      "quote": "In real GDP, which obr_shock reports, the q12 ratio is 0.33× (tiles: 0.21 after 1 year and 0.38 after 3 years in current prices, against the OBR's published 0.3; the run uses the current £6.55bn costing)",
      "basis": "site quote; the 1p basic-rate costing (£6.55bn/yr = £1,637.5m/q) held on household income for an explicit 12-quarter window, so the ratio does not depend on score_reform's default window. Ratio = −ΔGDP(£m) / 1,637.5 (the add-factor carries the revenue raised, so GDP falls). 0fe04c9 (October 2026 EFO, local run 18 Nov 2026; identical at 2965e82d) gives 0.330 (−540.2 at q12); 6fbbe06 gave 0.330 on £1,615.75m, e4d7faa 0.342, 1ed742c 0.357 (this is real GDP per current-price pound; the like-for-like current-price ratio is 0.376, obr #63/#66)",
      "checks": [
        {
          "name": "gdp_per_revenue_q12",
          "path": [
            "results",
            11,
            "delta_gdp_bn"
          ],
          "scale": -0.6106870229007634,
          "expected": 0.33,
          "tolerance": 0.01
        }
      ],
      "quoted_anchor": "<strong>0.33&times;</strong>",
      "via_job": true
    },
